# Healthcare & Life Sciences guardrails

When working in the `healthcare/` domain:

## Mandatory disclaimer

Every recipe README, model README, and examples README must include:
```markdown
> **Research / engineering use only.** Not for clinical or diagnostic use.
```

## PHI prohibition

- Never commit patient-identifiable data, protected health information (PHI), or internal hospital artifacts
- Use only public benchmarks (e.g. NSCLC-Radiomics via MONAI, ChEMBL, QM9, GEOM-Drugs), toy examples, or synthetic data
- If a user provides real patient data paths, warn them not to commit those paths to the repository

## Intended use

- Copy the "Intended Use" and "Limitations" sections from the upstream model card into the model README
- Never imply clinical applicability beyond what the model card states
- Drug discovery models (GP-MoLFormer, REINVENT4, SemlaFlow) generate candidate molecules for research — not approved therapeutics
